= 1920 <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Partito Popolare Italiano</span> Congress

The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Partito Popolare Italiano</span>, known also as the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">PPI</span> or the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#87CEFA;">Italian People's Party</span>y have begun their second Congress. The party has developed significantly over the past year, and a new face has emerged within the party: Alcide De Gasperi.

While Sturzo commands the support of the Christian Democrats and the 'White' <span style="color:#C0DCED;">Peasant Leagues</span>, De Gasperi is supported by Moderate Clericalists and the Clergy.

- @ppi_first: The party votes...

@ppi_first
go-to: sturzo_1920 if ppi_left >= ppi_moderates; gasperi_1920 if ppi_moderates > ppi_left

@sturzo_1920
face-image: img/portraits/LuigiSturzo.jpg
on-arrival: ppi_left += 2;

Unsurprisingly, Luigi Sturzo continues his leadership over the party, continuing the party's collaborative policies with the left.

@gasperi_1920
face-image: img/portraits/DeGasperi.jpg
on-arrival: ppi_relation -= 7; ppi_leader = "De Gasperi"; ppi_moderates += 2;

Surprisingly, Alcide De Gasperi, with his support base, has been elected the second Secretary General of the Party. He represents a turn from the left, seeking further cooperation with the <span style="color:#0047AB;">libe</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">ral</span> parties.